@startbpmn BP18_PlanAProjectsCourse
lang en

output L1 "01_detailed/BP18_PlanAProjectsCourse.bpmn"
output L2 "02_detailed/BP18_PlanAProjectsCourse.bpmn"

' Provenance (never in a drawn note, lint rule 5):
'   - a dependency is ENTERED, not drawn: how the user says what waits for what is the surface's
'     business and may be a form as much as a line pulled between two nodes, so the step names the
'     act - add an edge between two activities - and never the gesture: BR-99,
'     SA 2026-10-18 ("how do you know dependencies are drawn?")
'   - the edge removal commits on its own step, which IS the confirmation a deletion keeps, and it
'     carries the act's own word rather than Confirm: DRW-28, BR-20, SA 2026-10-18
'   - setting an activity Done while cards on its board are still open DISCLOSES them and asks what
'     becomes of them - close them with it, set them aside, or leave them open - because the state
'     is the planner's judgement and not a claim about every card. Where nothing is open the
'     disclosure is empty, and reopening takes nothing - so a Todo or InProgress change never puts
'     the question: BR-127, BR-109, SA 2026-10-11
'   - WHAT BECOMES OF THE OPEN TASKS IS A FIELD OF THE REQUEST, not a sub-flow of its own. The
'     three answers BR-127 names - close them with the activity, set them aside, leave them open -
'     differ only in what the one request carries, which the chain already records ("do with the
'     open tasks what the request carries"), so the guard and the three-way choice in front of the
'     submit are folded into the act that submits it. Same reasoning as the priority ruling of
'     2026-10-16: a value with no consequence beyond the record it travels in earns no box. The
'     disclosure POL-03 asks for is untouched - the impact read in front of the submit carries it.
'     BP11 was folded in the same pass: SA 2026-10-18 ("Apply first recommendation, also to BP18")
'   - an activity belongs to exactly one project and activities are flat: BR-98
'   - activities exist in an activity-based project only: BR-97, BR-105
'   - activities are created on the Course page, never on a board: BR-105
'   - a board is identified by its owner, an activity among the three: BR-101
'   - dependencies are finish-to-start and only within one project: BR-99
'   - an edge that would close a cycle is refused, naming the path: BR-100
'   - a deleted edge is never reconnected transitively: BR-104
'   - the Course page owns an activity's state alone; completion is offered: BR-109
'   - a Done activity can be reopened: BR-109
'   - an unfinished predecessor is flagged, never blocking: BR-110
'   - a plan orders and tracks; it never schedules: BR-111
'   - an activity deletion takes its tasks and is approve-or-abandon: BR-104, BR-113
'   - activities with no hand-made order list by dependency, then by name: BR-119, BR-120
'   - an activity is archived only with its project, never on its own: BR-23, BR-112
'   - the archive is no shield from a deletion: BR-117
'   - unfinished input is a draft, forms included: the field drafts as it is filled in, and the
'     operation that keeps it is drawn ONCE, in BP19, not per editing process. Here it is a
'     bound rule on the step that fills the field: BR-121, SA 2026-10-11
'   - one editor per entity: adding an activity and changing one are the same act, so there is
'     one editor node, one submit and one request. Call site BP18.03 (Amend an activity) is
'     RETIRED and its id never reused. The board is ENSURED rather than created, so the one
'     chain serves both: UX-04, DRW-11, SA 2026-10-14, ADR-066
'   - a deletion that discloses nothing still commits on a confirmation, so the step that
'     commits it reads as the confirmation, exactly as a disclosed deletion's does: DRW-28,
'     BR-20
'   - a step never enumerates the fields a request stores: which fields the entity carries is
'     a Detail Design matter and is not known yet, so the step names the act and its subject
'     only: SA 2026-10-14
'   - the box carries the act's own word, not the generic edit: the user DEFINES an activity:
'     SA 2026-10-16
'   - NOTHING IS FETCHED HERE. Every record is loaded once, at start-up (BP01), so a step that only
'     went to the store is gone, and one that selects or qualifies what the act works on says so
'     instead of saying read. What a chain still asks the system for is what it COMPUTES, which is
'     business and stays out of the client. When data is read is a detail design decision:
'     BR-128, DRW-14, SA 2026-10-17 ("when we will read data is not a business concern, but a
'     detail design decision ... I rule that this will be done once at startup")
'
' Scope: this process lays out and tracks one project's work. The project itself - creating it,
' amending it, archiving it, deleting it - is BP17, which hands over here by opening its course.
' Working an activity's board is BP11, and this process never touches a task's column; what it
' does answer is the activity's own state, which is also where BP11's completion offer lands.
'
' Call-site history: the plan was drawn inside BP17 until 2026-10-10 and moved here on the
' Software Architect's ruling, so that the project and its plan are one process each. BP17.06 to
' BP17.13 are retired there and are never reused.
'
' Call-site collapsing: setting an activity to Todo, to InProgress and to Done are variations of
' one request, and so is reopening a Done one.

pool "User" {
  start "A plan to lay out, or work to move on"
  :Work the plan;
  rule BR-118

  if "Which part of the plan?" then "add an activity, or change one"
    :Define the activity;
    rule BR-121
    :Submit the activity;
    send "Edit an activity" to actEditIn
    receive "The editing outcome" as actCreated
    note "An activity-based project only. A new activity is what brings its board into existence. The state is not edited here: it is set by its own request."
    end "Activity recorded"
  elseif "Which part of the plan?" then "move one along, or reopen it"
    :Set the activity's state;
    send "See what the state change takes" to stateImpactIn
    receive "What the change will take" as stateImpact
    :Submit the state change, saying what becomes of the tasks still open;
    rule BR-127
    rule BR-23
    rule BR-61
    send "Set an activity's state" to stateIn
    receive "The state-change outcome" as stateSet
    note "What the change takes is disclosed before it is submitted, and where tasks are still open the answer travels with the request: close them with the activity, set them aside, or leave them open. Where nothing is open there is nothing to answer."
    end "Activity state set"
  elseif "Which part of the plan?" then "say what waits for what"
    :Add a dependency between two activities;
    send "Add a dependency" to depAddIn
    receive "The dependency outcome" as depAdded
    note "Finish-to-start, and only between activities of this project."
    end "Dependency added"
  elseif "Which part of the plan?" then "drop a dependency"
    :Remove a dependency;
    send "Remove a dependency" to depRemoveIn
    receive "The removal outcome" as depRemoved
    end "Dependency dropped"
  elseif "Which part of the plan?" then "remove an activity"
    :Delete an activity;
    send "See what deleting an activity takes" to actImpactIn
    receive "What the activity deletion will take" as actImpact
    if "Approve what the deletion takes?" rule BR-104 then "approve"
      :Select a valid cascading option;
      rule BR-19
      :Confirm the deletion;
      send "Delete an activity" to actDeleteIn
      receive "The deletion outcome" as actDeleted
    else "reject"
      end "Deletion abandoned"
    endif
    end "Activity deleted"
  endif
}

system pool "Bearing" {
  messageStart "Activity submitted" as actEditIn
  call "BP18.02_CreateActivity" "Edit an activity" {
    :Store the edit;
    rule BR-98
    rule BR-105
    :Give a new activity its board;
    rule BR-101
    rule BR-65
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The editing outcome" to actCreated
  note "Activities are flat: finer granularity means more activities, never sub-activities. A board exists because its owner exists."
  end "Activity answered"

  messageStart "State-change impact requested" as stateImpactIn
  call "BP18.10_ReadTheStateChangeImpact" "See what the state change takes" {
    :Report which of the activity's tasks are still open, and what may become of them;
    rule BR-127
    rule BR-109
  }
  send "What the change will take" to stateImpact
  end "State-change impact answered"

  messageStart "Activity state submitted" as stateIn
  call "BP18.04_SetAnActivitysState" "Set an activity's state" {
    :Record the state the request names, and do with the open tasks what the request carries;
    rule BR-109
    rule BR-127
    rule BR-23
    :Report the outcome, and what the change clears or raises elsewhere;
    rule BR-110
  }
  send "The state-change outcome" to stateSet
  note "This is also where the board's completion offer lands."
  end "Activity state answered"

  messageStart "Dependency submitted" as depAddIn
  call "BP18.07_AddDependency" "Add a dependency" {
    if "Would the edge close a cycle?" rule BR-100 then "yes"
      :Refuse the edge and name the path it would close;
    else "no"
      :Store the finish-to-start edge within the project;
      rule BR-99
    endif
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The dependency outcome" to depAdded
  note "No start-to-start, no lag, no overlap, and no edge to another project's activity."
  end "Dependency answered"

  messageStart "Dependency removal requested" as depRemoveIn
  call "BP18.08_RemoveDependency" "Remove a dependency" {
    :Delete the dependency;
    rule BR-99
    rule BR-104
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The removal outcome" to depRemoved
  end "Dependency removal answered"

  messageStart "Activity deletion impact requested" as actImpactIn
  call "BP18.05_ReadTheActivityDeletionImpact" "See what deleting an activity takes" {
    :Report what the deletion will take, and what of it can be declined;
    rule BR-12
    rule BR-19
    rule BR-113
    rule BR-104
    rule BR-117
  }
  send "What the activity deletion will take" to actImpact
  note "A task needs a board, so declining has no legal outcome: the gesture is approved or abandoned. The dependency edges simply go."
  end "Activity impact answered"

  messageStart "Activity deletion requested" as actDeleteIn
  call "BP18.06_DeleteActivity" "Delete an activity" {
    :Delete confirmed items;
    rule BR-101
    rule BR-104
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The deletion outcome" to actDeleted
  note "The gap an edge leaves is not closed transitively. An activity is never archived on its own; only its project's archiving takes it."
  end "Activity deletion answered"
}

@endbpmn
